    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "net: check network activity in ThreadOpenConnections",
    "user": {
      "login": "naiyoma",
      "id": 40592031,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQwNTkyMDMx",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40592031?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/naiyoma",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Seednodes are used for addr-fetch connections. When the network is disabled (`networkactive=0` or `setnetworkactive false`), the seednodes are consumed without ever being dialled and  When the network becomes active again, no further addr-fetch attempts are made, even though the seednodes are still configured. They remain unavailable until the node is restarted.\n\nThis happens because `ThreadOpenConnections()`, continues running its loop while the network is disabled. With < 2 outbound peers or an empty addrman, a seednode is popped from `seed_nodes` , queued as an addr-fetch, and then popped again from `m_addr_fetches` in `ProcessAddrFetch()`. It is then dropped because `OpenNetworkConnection()` returns early when the network is inactive. Once the network is re-enabled, no seednodes remain. Anchors were lost in the same way before #34213.\n\n\nThis change makes `ThreadOpenConnections` wait while the network is re-enabled, as the way `ThreadPrivateBroadcast` does, so no connection state is used up while the network is disabled\n\n",
